{title: Silent Night, Holy Night}
{artist: Joseph Mohr (1818); tr. John F. Young (1859)}
{key: C}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 6/8}
{meta: tune STILLE NACHT - Franz X. Gruber (1818)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1859, tune 1818: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Silent night, holy night,
[G]All is calm, [C]all is bright
[F]Round yon virgin [C]mother and child.
[F]Holy infant so [C]tender and mild,
[G]Sleep in heavenly [C]peace, sleep in [G]heavenly [C]peace.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Silent night, holy night,
[G]Shepherds quake [C]at the sight;
[F]Glories stream from [C]heaven afar,
[F]Heavenly hosts sing [C]Alleluia!
[G]Christ, the Savior, is [C]born! Christ, the [G]Savior, is [C]born!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Silent night, holy night,
[G]Son of God, [C]love's pure light;
[F]Radiant beams from [C]Thy holy face
[F]With the dawn of re[C]deeming grace,
[G]Jesus, Lord, at Thy [C]birth, Jesus, [G]Lord, at Thy [C]birth.
{end_of_verse}
